===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|chemical test with acid}}{{lb|en|chemistry}} A [[test#Noun|test]] [[involve|involving]] the [[reaction#Noun|reaction]] of an [[acid#Noun|acid]] with another [[chemical#Noun|chemical]].
# {{senseid|en|rigorous test, figuratively}}{{lb|en|figuratively}} A [[rigorous#Adjective|rigorous]] test or [[appraisal#Noun|appraisal]] of the [[quality#Noun|quality]] or [[worth#Noun|worth]] of something.
#: {{cot|en|litmus test#English:_bar for persons, figuratively}}
#* {{RQ:Vance Destroying Angel|chapter=The Spy|page=152|passage=[H]e reflected that few professional beauties could have stood, as this woman did, the '''acid test''' of that mercilessly brilliant morning.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Stefanie Foster|title=Comment: Safety First: Now More than Ever|magazine=[[w:Rail (magazine)|Rail]]|location=Peterborough, Cambridgeshire|publisher=[[w:Bauer Media Group|Bauer Media]]|date=20 May 2020|page=3|issn=0953-4563|oclc=999467860|passage=The '''acid test''': will the British public abide by such stringent guidelines about where they should stand, walk or sit in our stations and on our trains, when they have been used to a turn-up-and-go railway where they enjoyed freedom having bought their ticket?}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Phil McNulty|authorlink=Phil McNulty|title=European Championship&nbsp;– Semi-final: [[w:England national football team|England]] 2&nbsp;– 1 [[w:Denmark national football team|Denmark]]|work={{w|BBC Sport}}|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230412194401/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/51198755|date=July 7 2021|passage=This was the '''acid test'''&nbsp;– at least before Sunday's final with formidable Italy&nbsp;– and they came up with the goods not only in the context of Euro 2020 but also in demonstrating their character and big match mentality.}}
# {{senseid|en|LSD party}}{{lb|en|by extension|historical}} In the 1960s, a [[party#Noun|party]] [[base#Verb|based]] around the [[use#Noun|use]] and [[advocacy]] of the [[psychedelic#Adjective|psychedelic]] [[drug#Noun|drug]] [[LSD#Noun|LSD]] (known in [[slang#Noun|slang]] as {{m|en|acid}}).

